    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0290" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./185: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-18T16:00:00+03:00">February 18,
                            1935—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 18—11:51 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. My 56, February 9, 1 p.m. Saturday afternoon<anchor n="13" xml:id="d195-f1"/>
                    Litvinov received Duranty. He showed him in “confidence” the undated memorandum
                    initialed by the President relative to settlement of debts and claims and
                    vigorously attacked American policy. He rejected Duranty’s suggestion to permit
                    publication of memorandum in <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> but I
                    understand that the Foreign Office censorship passed a despatch from Duranty
                    based on his conversation with Litvinov which was of a provocative nature. The
                    despatch was presumably published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi> this
                        morning.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d195-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The American correspondents are urging me to hold regular press conferences. I
                    would be grateful if the Department would indicate to me the attitude to adopt
                    when queried regarding “unpublished documents”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
